The models that can take a document as input in a chat message are `mistral-small-latest` (and by extension, other models supporting the same document input format). You pass the document by encoding it in base64 and including it in the `content` array of a user message with `type: "document_url"` and the `document_url` set to `data:application/pdf;base64,<base64_pdf>`. Example cURL request:

```bash
curl https://api.mistral.ai/v1/chat/completions \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer ${MISTRAL_API_KEY}" \
  -d '{
    "model": "mistral-small-latest",
    "messages": [
      {
        "role": "user",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "what is the last sentence in the document"
          },
          {
            "type": "document_url",
            "document_url": "data:application/pdf;base64,<base64_pdf>"
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }'
